  "seoBody": "<h2>What is care home compliance software in Scotland?</h2><p>In Scotland the Care Inspectorate regulates care homes. CQC applies in England only. So compliance software for a Scottish home should be built around the Health and Social Care Standards and the Care Inspectorate quality framework How good is our care and support?, not the English system. That framework organises evaluation into key questions: how good is our care and support, how good is our setting, how good is our staffing, and how good is our leadership. Each breaks into quality indicators, and a home grades itself on a six-point scale from 1 unsatisfactory to 6 excellent.</p><p>Care home compliance software helps a home run the recurring audits behind those grades, honestly and continuously, and hold the evidence for each. Quickler does this as WhatsApp workflows with one dashboard across your homes.</p><h2>The recurring audits a Scottish home carries</h2><p>The recurring set is medication storage and administration, infection prevention and control, falls and moving-and-handling, hoists under LOLER, fire and legionella awareness, adult support and protection, care plan reviews, training and supervision, and kitchen and food hygiene. Some are daily or weekly, such as medication fridge temperatures and kitchen checks. Some are monthly, such as the infection control walk. Some are quarterly or on a rolling review, such as care plans and adult support and protection. Some are event-driven, such as an incident record.</p><p>Scotland-specific law matters here. Adult safeguarding is under the Adult Support and Protection (Scotland) Act 2007, known as adult support and protection or ASP. Fire safety is under the Fire (Scotland) Act 2005 and the Fire Safety (Scotland) Regulations 2006, not the English fire safety order. Certain events are notifiable to the Care Inspectorate, and RIDDOR still applies UK-wide to the HSE for work-related incidents. Always work from the current published law.</p><h2>How quickler runs it</h2><p>Quickler turns a recurring audit or a whole key question into a workflow that runs over the WhatsApp Business API. The registered manager or a nominated staff member walks the home and answers each prompt in their existing WhatsApp chat, with text, a voice note or a photo tied to the indicator it evidences. Voice notes are transcribed automatically. The report and improvement plan generate themselves, and a group running several registered homes sees each one's position on a single dashboard.</p><h2>Pricing</h2><p>Pricing is only for active users: [[price:bundles]]. An active user is someone who completed at least two workflows that month, so you can add every manager, nurse, care worker and bank worker across the group and pay only for who actually files something. The free tier is 20 reports a month and up to 10 photos per report, no card and no trial clock.</p><h2>What quickler is not</h2><p>Quickler is not a care record, care management, eMAR or clinical system, and holds no resident care data. It captures the audit walk and the evidence around it: photos of the setting, observations against quality indicators, the state of records at the point of check. For medication and care plans it records that the check was done and captures the evidence, without copying a resident's personal or clinical data into quickler. Personal plans, medication administration records and personal care logs stay in your care planning system, which remains the single source of truth. Quickler is the audit and evidence layer that sits alongside the care system.</p><p>Quickler is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Care Inspectorate, and whether your evidence satisfies an inspection is a judgement for you and your inspector. This page is general information, not regulatory advice; always work from the current published framework, standards and law.</p><h2>Related guides</h2><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/care-inspectorate-compliance-software-scotland.html\">Care Inspectorate compliance software Scotland</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/care-inspectorate-self-evaluation-scotland.html\">Care Inspectorate self-evaluation</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/care-inspectorate-mock-inspection-checklist-scotland.html\">Care Inspectorate mock inspection checklist</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/care-inspectorate-grades-explained-scotland.html\">Care Inspectorate grades explained</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/care-home-compliance-software-uk.html\">Care home compliance software UK</a></li></ul>",
